<header><h1>The Titans of Ul: Proof</h1></header>
<article>
<p>The source text behind each note on <a href="/F_ul">The Titans of Ul</a>. <b>Explicit</b> sources state the note directly. <b>Implicit</b> sources support it without stating it.</p>

<h2 id="terragenesis"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Titans_of_Ul#Faction_Abilities:~:text=Terragenesis">Terragenesis</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>A planet cannot contain more than one sleeper token.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Which side of the sleeper token is used &hellip;?&rdquo;: &ldquo;A planet holds one sleeper.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Can Titans put more than one sleeper on a planet with Terragenesis &hellip;?&rdquo;: &ldquo;a planet holds at most one.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The Ul player may only move a sleeper token with <sc>Terragenesis</sc> once all of their sleeper tokens are on the game board.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Which side of the sleeper token is used, when does Terragenesis move one, and can Awaken work with no PDS left?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Terragenesis moves one only once all yours are on the board.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="awaken"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Titans_of_Ul#Faction_Abilities:~:text=Awaken">Awaken</a> <sub></sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>Only sleeper tokens present in the system when it is activated may be replaced with PDS.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;When can the Titans use Awaken, and can Ceasefire or Nullification Field stop it?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Right after activating a system that already held your sleeper token.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>A sleeper token that is placed during the <b>Activation</b> step, most commonly by using the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Cybernetic_Technologies#Scanlink_Drone_Network"><i>Scanlink Drone Network</i></a> technology and the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Titans_of_Ul#Faction_Abilities:~:text=Terragenesis"><sc>Terragenesis</sc></a> ability, cannot be replaced via the <sc>Awaken</sc> ability during the same tactical action.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;When can the Titans use Awaken, and can Ceasefire or Nullification Field stop it?&rdquo;: &ldquo;a sleeper placed later in that activation, say by Scanlink exploration, can&rsquo;t be awakened then.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The Ul player may place a PDS on a planet that contains two of another player&rsquo;s PDS. They cannot place a PDS on a planet that already contains two of their own PDS.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Does 63.3 (2 PDS on a planet max) mean that Titans couldn&rsquo;t place a PDS via Sleeper token onto a planet where another player already has 2 PDS? &hellip; A: 63.3 does not prevent Titans from placing a PDS on a planet that contains 2 of another player&rsquo;s PDS units. You cannot place a structure on a planet with the maximum number of your structures.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the Ul player places a PDS on a planet controlled by another player, and that player has ground forces on that planet, then a ground combat will be resolved during the <b>Invasion</b> step of the tactical action.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the Ul player activates a system containing their sleeper tokens and the <a href="/F_xxcha">Xxcha</a> player&rsquo;s ships, the Ul player, as the active player, may resolve <sc>Awaken</sc> before the <a href="/F_xxcha">Xxcha</a> player resolves the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Xxcha_Kingdom#Faction_Technologies:~:text=Nullification%20Field"><i>Nullification Field</i></a> technology. Any resulting ground combat still occurs.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;When can the Titans use Awaken, and can Ceasefire or Nullification Field stop it?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Awaken and Nullification Field share the after-activation window, and the active Titans go first, so they can awaken before their turn is ended; the resulting ground combat still happens.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>A sleeper token is not removed when another player gains control of the planet it is on. The Ul player may still replace it using <sc>Awaken</sc>.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Is the Titans&rsquo; Hel Titan a ground force, and does a sleeper stay when another player takes the planet?&rdquo;: &ldquo;A sleeper token is only removed by Awaken or by the planet being destroyed, so it stays on a captured planet and can be awakened later.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the Ul player retreats into a system containing their sleeper token, <sc>Awaken</sc> is not triggered, as the system is not activated.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;If the Titans retreat into a system with a sleeper, does it awaken?&rdquo;: &ldquo;No &mdash; a retreat places a command token but doesn&rsquo;t activate the system.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If another player plays the Ul player&rsquo;s <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Promissory_Notes#Ceasefire"><i>Ceasefire</i></a> promissory note, the Ul player may still place units into the active system using their <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Titans_of_Ul#Faction_Abilities:~:text=Awaken"><sc>Awaken</sc></a> ability.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;When can the Titans use Awaken, and can Ceasefire or Nullification Field stop it?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Ceasefire only stops movement, so Awaken still works.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the Ul player wishes to place a PDS, but there are none left in their reinforcements, they may remove a PDS from any system that does not contain one of their command tokens and place that instead. The PDS will be placed undamaged.<sup>1,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR 23.4a: &ldquo;that player can remove a unit from any system that does not contain one of their command tokens and place that unit in their reinforcements.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;If a unit is damaged, and is &lsquo;removed and placed&rsquo; from the board via a game effect, does it come back repaired &hellip;? A: &hellip; If it is produced, placed, or replaced which would require a remove and place it is no longer damaged.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="coalescence"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Titans_of_Ul#Faction_Abilities:~:text=Coalescence">Coalescence</a> <sub></sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>Units placed on planets via the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Titans_of_Ul#Faction_Abilities:~:text=Awaken"><sc>Awaken</sc></a> ability are not committed. They cannot be assigned hits during the <b>Space Cannon Defense</b> step.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the Ul player&rsquo;s units exist in the same location as another player&rsquo;s units, effects that end the Ul player&rsquo;s turn cannot prevent the combat from occurring.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;If you awaken a sleeper token or deploy your flagship and then your turn ends (Mahact mech, Nullification field, Minister of Peace), do you resolve combat? A: Coalescence forces combat steps to occur.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Only the active player may use the <a href="/R_bombardment"><sc>Bombardment</sc></a> ability of their units during an invasion.<sup>3,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>3</sup> Learn to Play, Bombardment: &ldquo;A player uses this ability during the &lsquo;Bombardment&rsquo; step of an invasion.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;only the active player can use BOMBARDMENT.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol><li>This prevents the <a href="/F_lizix">L1Z1X</a> player from using their <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_L1Z1X_Mindnet#Faction_Abilities:~:text=Harrow"><sc>Harrow</sc></a> ability.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Can the L1Z1X use harrow when they&rsquo;re defending during ground combat? A: No, only the active player can use BOMBARDMENT.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li></ol>
    <li>If the Ul player&rsquo;s turn is ended by another game effect, the combat still occurs. No other steps of the tactical action occur, and abilities may only be used within that combat.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Coalescence forces combat steps to occur. No other steps of the tactical action occur, and abilities can only be used within combat.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="terraform"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Titans_of_Ul#Faction_Promissory_Note:~:text=Terraform">Terraform</a> <sub>(Promissory Note)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>Once played, <i>Terraform</i> is never returned to the Ul player.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Can the Titans play their own Terraform note, or reuse it after it&rsquo;s attached?&rdquo;: &ldquo;once attached it can&rsquo;t be played again or traded.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Once played, <i>Terraform</i> counts as being in the play area of the player who controls the planet.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Yes, when Terraform is attached to a planet it counts as being in that planet owner&rsquo;s play area.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol><li>If the Ul player gains control of a planet with <i>Terraform</i> attached, their own <i>Terraform</i> will be in their play area.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Yes, when Terraform is attached to a planet it counts as being in that planet owner&rsquo;s play area.&rdquo; Applies when the Ul player owns the planet.</li>
        </ul></li></ol>
    <li>If a planet has multiple traits, the player exploring the planet chooses which of the corresponding exploration decks to draw from.<sup>2,7</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>7</sup> Thunder&rsquo;s Edge Rulebook p. 11: &ldquo;Planets that have dual planet traits count as having both traits. When exploring one of these planets &hellip;, the exploring player can choose to draw a card matching either&rdquo; trait.</li>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR 35.2c: &ldquo;If a planet has multiple traits, the player exploring the planet chooses which of the corresponding exploration decks to draw from.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Which exploration deck do I draw from when a planet has more than one trait?&rdquo;: &ldquo;You choose one of the matching trait decks and draw a single card from it.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If <i>Terraform</i> is attached to a planet in The Fracture, that planet may be explored.<sup>6</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>6</sup> Community consensus: &ldquo;If Terraform is attached, can planets in The Fracture be explored? A: Yes&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li><i>Terraform</i> may be attached to <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Thunder&#x27;s_Edge">Thunder&rsquo;s Edge</a>.<sup>6</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>6</sup> Community consensus: &ldquo;Can Terraform be attached to Thunder&rsquo;s Edge? A: Yes.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="heltitan"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Titans_of_Ul#:~:text=Hel-Titan">Hel&ndash;Titan</a> <sub>(Unit)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>When multiple units use their <a href="/R_production"><sc>Production</sc></a> ability, the <a href="/R_production"><sc>Production</sc></a> value is pooled. As such, if the Ul player has two Hel&ndash;Titans in a system, they may produce two infantry or two fighters for one resource, rather than two resources.<sup>1,2,3</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR FAQ: &ldquo;Production value is totaled when the &lsquo;Production&rsquo; ability of units in a system is used.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>3</sup> Learn to Play: &ldquo;When producing multiple units at a time, the cost values of those units are added together.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Does Production limit the number of units or their total cost?&rdquo;: &ldquo;The number of units.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Effects that remove ground forces, and then place them on the game board without transporting them, such as the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Prophecy_of_Kings:~:text=Decoy%20Operation"><i>Decoy Operation</i></a> action card or the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Cybernetic_Technologies#Transit_Diodes"><i>Transit Diodes</i></a> technology, may be used on a Hel&ndash;Titan.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Can Transit Diodes move Titans Hel-Titans or ordinary PDS?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Hel-Titans yes: they are ground forces, and Transit Diodes removes and places units rather than transporting them.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Effects that move ground forces, such as the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Codex_I:~:text=Ghost%20Squad"><i>Ghost Squad</i></a> action card or the ability of the <a href="/F_norr">N&rsquo;orr</a> player&rsquo;s commander, <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Sardakk_N&#x27;orr#:~:text=G%27hom%20Sek%27kus">G&rsquo;hom Sek&rsquo;kus</a>, (via the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Promissory_Notes#Alliance"><i>Alliance</i></a> promissory note), cannot be used to move a Hel&ndash;Titan to another planet.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Can the Titans Hel-Titan move via abilities like the action card Ghost Squad or via the Sardakk N&rsquo;Orr Alliance? A: No, structures cannot move.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>A Hel&ndash;Titan is a structure, and so cannot be targeted by the <a href="/F_vuilraith">Vuil&rsquo;raith</a> player&rsquo;s <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Vuil&#x27;Raith_Cabal#:~:text=Vortex"><i>Vortex</i></a> faction technology.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Is a Hel-Titan a valid target for effects on non-structures &hellip;?&rdquo;: &ldquo;It is a structure as well as a ground force, so the Vuil&rsquo;raith vortex, which needs a non-structure, can&rsquo;t take it.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If a player is able to ignore <a href="/R_planetary_shield"><sc>Planetary Shield</sc></a>, then Hel&ndash;Titan are eligible units to assign any hits produced by a bombardment roll.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="saturn-engine"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Titans_of_Ul#Cruiser:~:text=Saturn%20Engine">Saturn Engine</a> <sub>(Unit)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    </ol>

<h2 id="ouranos"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Titans_of_Ul#Flagship:~:text=Ouranos">Ouranos</a> <sub>(Flagship)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>Only PDS present in the system when it is activated may be replaced with the <i>Ouranos</i>.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Can the Titans deploy their flagship for free &hellip;?&rdquo;: &ldquo;the PDS must be there when you activate.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>A PDS that is placed during the activation step, most commonly by using the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Titans_of_Ul#Faction_Abilities:~:text=Awaken"><sc>Awaken</sc></a> ability, cannot be replaced with the <i>Ouranos</i> during the same tactical action.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> Same entry: &ldquo;one placed by Awaken during that activation doesn&rsquo;t qualify.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="tellurian"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Titans_of_Ul#Leaders:~:text=Tellurian">Tellurian</a> <sub>(Agent)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>The timing of Tellurian is changed to &ldquo;before you assign a hit&rdquo;, the same as the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Twilight_Imperium_Fourth_Edition:~:text=Shields%20Holding"><i>Shields Holding</i></a> action card and the <a href="/R_sustain_damage"><sc>Sustain Damage</sc></a> ability. As such, if Tellurian cancels a hit produced by a player who owns the <a href="/F_norr">N&rsquo;orr</a> player&rsquo;s <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Sardakk_N&#x27;orr#:~:text=Valkyrie%20Particle%20Weave"><i>Valkyrie Particle Weave</i></a> technology, <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Sardakk_N&#x27;orr#:~:text=Valkyrie%20Particle%20Weave"><i>Valkyrie Particle Weave</i></a> still triggers before the hit is canceled.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;The Titan&rsquo;s Agent will receive an errata to have the same timing as Shields Holding or Sustain Damage. &lsquo;Before you assign a hit&rsquo;. The hit is still produced, VPW triggers, then the hit is canceled.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="tungstantus"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Titans_of_Ul#Leaders:~:text=Tungstantus">Tungstantus</a> <sub>(Commander)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>The trade good may be spent on the units produced by the <a href="/R_production"><sc>Production</sc></a> ability that triggered Tungstantus.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling, Ul commander Tungstantus: &ldquo;The gain and spend are simultaneous, so cannot be pillaged.&rdquo; gain and spend are simultaneous.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol>
        <li>The trade good may be spent as it is gained. The number of trade goods the Ul player has after producing units is used to determine if the <a href="/F_mentak">Mentak</a> player may use their <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Mentak_Coalition#Faction_Abilities:~:text=Pillage"><sc>Pillage</sc></a> ability.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling, Ul commander Tungstantus: &ldquo;The gain and spend are simultaneous, so cannot be pillaged.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
        <li>A trade good will not be gained unless at least one unit is produced.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>
    <li>Other effects that produce units without a unit using its <a href="/R_production"><sc>Production</sc></a> ability will not trigger Tungstantus.<sup>14</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>14</sup> Codex II, Ul Alliance: &ldquo;When 1 or more of your units use PRODUCTION: You may gain 1 trade good.&rdquo; trigger requires a unit using PRODUCTION.</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="ul-the-progenitor"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Titans_of_Ul#Leaders:~:text=Ul%20the%20Progenitor">Ul the Progenitor</a> &mdash; <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Titans_of_Ul#Faction_Specific_Components:~:text=Geoform">Geoform</a> <sub>(Hero)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>The <a href="/R_space_cannon"><sc>Space Cannon</sc></a> ability is controlled by whichever player controls Elysium.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Elysium counts as a planet with an attachment for objectives such as <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Objectives#Prophecy_of_Kings_Expansion_2:~:text=Reclaim%20Ancient%20Monuments"><i>Reclaim Ancient Monuments</i></a>.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found. Twilight Imperium Wiki FAQ (not a numbered source), Titans of Ul: &ldquo;Does the Geoform ability of Ul the progenitor count as an attachment for the purpose of the objective &lsquo;Reclaim ancient monuments&rsquo;? A: Yes&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="hecatoncheires"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Titans_of_Ul#Mech:~:text=Hecatoncheires">Hecatoncheires</a> <sub>(Mech)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>When the Ul player would place multiple PDS during a single step, they may resolve a <a href="/R_deploy"><sc>Deploy</sc></a> ability to place one Hecatoncheires for any or all of those PDS.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The Ul player must have at least one PDS in their reinforcements to place in order to use the <a href="/R_deploy"><sc>Deploy</sc></a> ability of a Hecatoncheires. However, when they would place a PDS, they may remove a PDS from any system that does not contain one of their command tokens and put it in their reinforcements. They may then use the <a href="/R_deploy"><sc>Deploy</sc></a> ability of a Hecatoncheires.<sup>1,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;You also cannot DEPLOY a mech if you have no PDS in reinforcements, but could remove a PDS from the board and then DEPLOY your mech to an eligible target planet.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR 30.2: &ldquo;A player can only resolve a deploy ability to place a unit that is in their reinforcements.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The Ul player cannot place a PDS on a planet that already has two of their PDS on it. As such, they are unable to place a Hecatoncheires on a planet with two of their PDS using its <a href="/R_deploy"><sc>Deploy</sc></a> ability.<sup>3,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Does 63.3 (2 PDS on a planet max) mean that Titans couldn&rsquo;t place a PDS via Sleeper token onto a planet where another player already has 2 PDS? &hellip; A: 63.3 does not prevent Titans from placing a PDS on a planet that contains 2 of another player&rsquo;s PDS units. You cannot place a structure on a planet with the maximum number of your structures.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Same ruling: &ldquo;which prevents using the DEPLOY ability on a planet with 2 PDS of yours.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>3</sup> Learn to Play: &ldquo;Players are limited to two PDS units and one space dock on each planet.&rdquo; The Deploy consequence is not stated.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>A <a href="/R_deploy"><sc>Deploy</sc></a> ability may only be resolved for units in a player&rsquo;s reinforcements. If all four of the Hecatoncheires are already on the board, no Hecatoncheires may be deployed.<sup>1,8</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR 30.2: &ldquo;A player can only resolve a deploy ability to place a unit that is in their reinforcements.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>8</sup> PoK rulebook p. 10: &ldquo;These abilities can only be resolved to place a unit that is in a player&rsquo;s reinforcements.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The Ul player may use the <a href="/R_deploy"><sc>Deploy</sc></a> ability of a Hecatoncheires to place units into coexistence, most often through the use of <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Titans_of_Ul#Breakthrough:~:text=Slumberstate%20Computing"><i>Slumberstate Computing</i></a>.<sup>6</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>6</sup> Community consensus: &ldquo;Can Titans use the Mech&rsquo;s deploy ability for coexistence? A: Yes.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The Ul player may use the <a href="/R_deploy"><sc>Deploy</sc></a> ability of a Hecatoncheires when placing a PDS with the <a href="/R_construction"><i>Construction</i></a> strategy card, including for each PDS placed with the primary ability.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Can the Titans deploy their mech instead of placing a PDS with Construction?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Yes &mdash; Construction places PDS, so the Titans&rsquo; deploy works there, even twice with the primary.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="slumberstate-computing"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Titans_of_Ul#Breakthrough:~:text=Slumberstate%20Computing">Slumberstate Computing</a> <sub>(Breakthrough)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>A planet controlled by another player may contain at most one sleeper token.<sup>2,6</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal: &ldquo;a planet holds at most one.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>6</sup> Community consensus, Slumberstate Computing, limit of Sleeper tokens on another player&rsquo;s planet: &ldquo;Is there a limit to the number of Sleeper tokens that may be placed on another player&rsquo;s planet? A: One per planet&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The Ul player does not have to be neighbors with the player that agrees to have a sleeper token placed on their planet.<sup>9</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>9</sup> Designer Q&amp;A, &ldquo;Titans Breakthrough&rdquo;: &ldquo;There is no real timing window or other requirement, it is something that can easily be worked into a transaction or deal with friendly players.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>There is no timing window or other requirement for another player allowing the Ul player to place a sleeper token on a planet they control; it may be included as part of a transaction or deal.<sup>9</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>9</sup> Same answer: &ldquo;There is no real timing window or other requirement, it is something that can easily be worked into a transaction or deal.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol><li>As such, allowing the Ul player to place a sleeper token can be part of a binding deal.<sup>1,9</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR 28.3: &ldquo;If the terms of a deal can be resolved immediately, it is a binding deal.&rdquo; The sleeper token can be placed immediately, with no timing window.</li>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>9</sup> Designer Q&amp;A, Titans Breakthrough: &ldquo;There is no real timing window or other requirement, it is something that can easily be worked into a transaction or deal with friendly players.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li></ol>
    <li>When another player agrees to allow the Ul player to place a sleeper token, the agreement includes which planet the token will be placed on.<sup>6</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>6</sup> Community consensus: &ldquo;Does the agreement to place a Sleeper token require agreeing to a specific planet &hellip;? A: Agreement includes which planet.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The additional action cards are only drawn during the <b>Draw Action Cards</b> step of the status phase. Other effects that draw action cards during the status phase, such as the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#Directives:~:text=Minister%20of%20Policy"><i>Minister of Policy</i></a> agenda or the <a href="/F_mentak">Mentak</a> player&rsquo;s agent, <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Mentak_Coalition#Leaders:~:text=Suffi%20An">Suffi An</a>, do not draw additional action cards.<sup>6</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>6</sup> Community consensus: &ldquo;Does that mean that you&rsquo;ll be receiving additional AC for the Minister of Policy &hellip;? A: No, the ability is specifically Status Phase Step 3 Draw Action Cards.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>
